"""
A cross-reference identifier for a specification document.

Every relationship between documents is expressed as a slug rather than a
path, so moving a file never breaks a reference. Slugs are kebab-case:
lowercase alphanumeric words joined by single hyphens.
"""
alias Slug: String ~= /^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/

"""
A reference to another specification document, optionally qualified by
an anchor into one of its sections.

Held apart from `Slug` because the two type different things: `Slug` is
the identity a document declares about itself, and admitting an anchor
there would let a document declare its identity as `adr-012#Decision`,
breaking uniqueness and slug resolution. A citation names someone
else's identity and may legitimately point at a place inside it — the
slug half matches the same pattern `Slug` does, and a trailing `#` with
nothing after it is rejected rather than admitted as an anchor-less
citation.
"""
alias Citation: String ~= /^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*(?:#.+)?$/

"""
The classification of a specification document.

A document's type selects the schema, slug pattern and required sections
that govern it. This is the controlled vocabulary the specs
profile registers; a repository whose documents declare a type outside
this set is recorded as excluded with reason `unknown-type` rather than
being checked against the wrong rules.
"""
enum DocumentType {
  """An architecture decision record: one decision, its alternatives and its consequences."""
  Adr: "adr"

  """A feature requirements document: the user-facing need and its acceptance criteria."""
  Frd: "frd"

  """An interface specification shared across a boundary of independent change."""
  Contract: "contract"

  """Cross-cutting standards, policies, guidelines or constraints."""
  Standards: "standards"

  """A C4 system blueprint: the containers a system bundles and the contracts it provides."""
  SystemBlueprint: "system-blueprint"

  """A C4 container blueprint: one deployable artifact and the modules composed into it."""
  ContainerBlueprint: "container-blueprint"

  """A C4 module blueprint: a coherent unit of code with its own interface."""
  ModuleBlueprint: "module-blueprint"

  """A C4 component blueprint: a single component promoted to its own document."""
  ComponentBlueprint: "component-blueprint"

  """A transient change document describing how the system changes to deliver one feature."""
  FeatureBlueprint: "feature-blueprint"

  """An improvement proposal raised against a skill by a run that exercised it."""
  Rfc: "rfc"

  """A how-to document explaining a technique the other document types assume."""
  Guide: "guide"
}

"""
How badly a run was impeded by the skill an RFC critiques.

An RFC carries the highest severity among its proposals, so that triage
can rank a queue without opening every document.
"""
enum RfcSeverity {
  """Forced an unscripted improvisation, or the skill as written produced a wrong result."""
  Blocker: "blocker"

  """The skill was silent on a decision that materially changed the outcome."""
  Snag: "snag"

  """It worked, but a change would make the next run clearer, faster, or safer."""
  Polish: "polish"
}

"""
The lifecycle state of a document.

State documents — blueprints, standards and contracts, which describe
what IS — use `active` and never `in-progress`. Transient change
documents, which describe a change, use `in-progress` in its place: a
change specification is implemented, not put into effect.
"""
enum Status {
  """Under authorship; content may be incomplete."""
  Draft: "draft"

  """Complete and awaiting review."""
  ReadyForReview: "ready-for-review"

  """Reviewed and accepted; not yet in effect."""
  Approved: "approved"

  """Approved, and the change it specifies is being implemented."""
  InProgress: "in-progress"

  """In effect; the current source of truth."""
  Active: "active"

  """No longer in effect. A retired document names its replacement in `superseded_by`."""
  Retired: "retired"
}

"""
Whether an interface or module is published beyond the repository that
declares it.

Visibility governs the compatibility obligation, not the access
modifier: a public surface owes adopters a versioning policy, while an
internal one may change in lockstep with its only consumers.
"""
enum Visibility {
  """Published for consumption outside this repository; bound by its versioning policy."""
  Public: "public"

  """Unpublished and in-repo; evolves in lockstep with its consumers."""
  Internal: "internal"
}

"""
Whether a blueprint documents one concrete element or a pattern that
several elements follow.
"""
enum BlueprintKind {
  """One concrete element, documented in its own right."""
  Standard: "standard"

  """A repeated shape that several elements instantiate."""
  Pattern: "pattern"
}

"""
The delivery unit a feature blueprint is groomed against.
"""
enum Delivery {
  """The whole feature lands in one pull request."""
  SinglePr: "single-pr"

  """The feature lands across several stages, each boundary enumerated in Sequencing Constraints."""
  Staged: "staged"
}
